  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0188 database is designed to manage various aspects of a hospital's operations. It contains eight tables: DEPARTMENTS, EMPLOYEES, SCHEDULES, HOSPITAL_RESOURCES, PATIENTS, CASES, HANDLES, and HOUSED_UNDER. The DEPARTMENTS table stores information about the hospital's departments, including their IDs, available rooms, locations, number of employees, and budgets. Each employee is represented in the EMPLOYEES table, which includes their first name, middle initial, last name, position, address, salary, and department ID, with a composite primary key combining their ID and department ID to ensure each employee is uniquely associated with a department. The SCHEDULES table tracks the shifts worked by employees, including the start and end times, employee ID, and date, with a primary key combining the employee ID and shift ID to prevent duplicate schedules for the same employee. The HOSPITAL_RESOURCES table lists the hospital's supplies, including their names, types, counts, and department IDs, with a primary key combining the supply name and department ID to ensure each supply is uniquely associated with a department. The PATIENTS table stores patient information, including their first name, middle initial, last name, social security number, patient ID, date of birth, address, and insurance details, with a primary key combining the social security number and patient ID to uniquely identify each patient. The CASES table tracks patient cases, including case IDs, room numbers, admitting physicians, prescriptions, patient IDs, admission and discharge dates, with a primary key combining the case ID and patient ID to prevent duplicate cases for the same patient. The HANDLES table links employees to cases they are handling, with a primary key combining the employee ID and case ID to ensure each employee is uniquely associated with a case. Finally, the HOUSED_UNDER table tracks patients who are being housed under a specific department for a particular case, with a primary key combining the patient ID, department ID, and case ID to ensure each patient is uniquely associated with a department and case.",
  "gold_question": "Hospital Management System\n\n1) Background / Context\nThe project aims to develop a database management system (DBMS) for efficient hospital management. The system should support the organization of hospital departments, employee scheduling, resource allocation, and patient care, ensuring seamless operation and optimal resource use.\n\n2) Objectives\n- To manage and organize departments based on budget and resources.\n- To maintain comprehensive employee records and schedules.\n- To record and track patient cases, treatments, and departmental assignments.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n- Hospital Administrators\n- Department Heads\n- Medical Staff (Doctors, Nurses, Technicians)\n- Support Staff (Receptionists, Pharmacists, Sanitary Workers)\n- Patients\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n- Department Management: Maintain records of departments including location, available rooms, number of employees, and budget. Manage resources such as medical equipment and office supplies.\n- Employee Management: Record employee details (name, position, address, salary) and track their departmental assignments. Schedule employee shifts with start and end times.\n- Patient Management: Document patient information (name, DOB, insurance) and track their medical history and current cases. Manage case assignments and associated resources.\n- Case Management: Assign medical staff to patient cases based on specialization. Record details such as prescriptions, actions taken, and admittance information.\n- Resource Management: Track hospital resources by department, including availability and type.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- The system should ensure data security and privacy, especially concerning patient information.\n- It should be scalable to accommodate additional departments, employees, and patients.\n- The DBMS should provide reliable uptime and robust performance to support hospital operations.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0188.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0188\nCREATE TABLE `departments` (\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `available_rooms` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `number_of_employees` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `budget` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`department_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employees` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_initial` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `salary` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`, `department_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employees_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `departments` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `schedules` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `shift_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `date` date NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`, `shift_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `schedules_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employees` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `hospital_resources` (\n  `supply_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `supply_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `count` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`supply_name`, `department_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `hospital_resources_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `departments` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `patients` (\n  `social_security_number` char(9) NOT NULL,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `first_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `middle_initial` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `last_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `insurance_details` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`social_security_number`, `patient_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `cases` (\n  `case_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `room_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `admitting_physician` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `prescriptions` text NOT NULL,\n  `admission_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `discharge_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`case_id`, `patient_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `cases_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patients` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `handles` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `case_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`, `case_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `handles_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employees` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `handles_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`case_id`) REFERENCES `cases` (`case_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `housed_under` (\n  `patient_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `case_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`patient_id`, `department_id`, `case_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `housed_under_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`patient_id`) REFERENCES `patients` (`patient_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `housed_under_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `departments` (`department_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `housed_under_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`case_id`) REFERENCES `cases` (`case_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
